---
title: Machine Chest Press
type: docs
prev: docs/grud/
---
![](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e6c69aa8-ce8f-45c1-8294-f5446737b4cc)


{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Adjust the seat height so the handles are aligned with your mid-to-lower chest. Sit up tall with a slight arch in your lower back, pull your shoulders down, and squeeze your shoulder blades together. Rest the back of your head against the backrest and place your feet flat on the floor directly under your knees.

### Step 2
Grip the handles slightly wider than shoulder-width with an overhand grip, keeping your wrists straight and aligned with your forearms.

### Step 3
Exhale and press the handles forward away from your chest.

### Step 4
Pause briefly at the end of the push (without locking your elbows), then inhale and slowly return the handles to the starting position.

### Step 5
Once the handles get close to your chest, immediately begin the next rep without resting.

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
• Do not use momentum—keep the movement slow and controlled through the full range of motion.

• Keep your elbows pointing out to the sides and push smoothly.

• Maintain a steady breathing rhythm throughout the set.
{{< /callout >}}
